  "solution": "The logic followed in the given sets is:\n\n**(First term + Third term) × 4 = Second term**\n\nNow we apply the pattern on the given sets:\n\n(13, 84, 8) \n\n(__**13 + 8**__) × 4 = 84\n\n__**21 × 4**__ = 84 \n\n84 = 84\n\n(21, 136, 13)\n\n__**(21 + 13)**__ × 4 =136\n\n__**34 **____**× 4**__ = 136\n\n136 = 136\n\nNow we apply the pattern on the given options:\n\nOption 1) (14, 56, 8)\n\n(__14 + 8__) × 4 = 56\n\n__22 × 4__ = 56\n\n88 ≠ 56\n\nOption 2) (16, 23, 156)\n\n(__16 + 156__) × 4 = 23\n\n__172 × 4__ = 23\n\n688 ≠ 23\n\nOption 3) (8, 71, 19)\n\n(__8 + 19__) × 4 = 71\n\n__27 × 4__ = 71\n\n108 ≠ 71\n\nOption 4) **(27, 140, 8) **\n\n(__**27 + 8**__)** **× 4 = 140\n\n__**35 × 4**__ = 140\n\n**140 = 140**\n\nHence, the correct answer is **Option 4.**",
